; -- group c155 --
; [new] card "long_tom(eng)" cost 1000 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x2 | vehicles longtom_155mm | tags all artillery heavyart heavy 43 44 45 | units/eng/vehicles_45.set:54 | {info longtom_155mm}; also under usa/v22; cards long_tom(eng), longtom_155mm(usa); copy of longtom_155mm (with crew)
{"longtom_155mm" "Before entering World War I, the United States was poorly equipped with heavy artillery. To address this problem a number of foreign heavy artillery guns were adopted, including the Canon de 155 mm GPF. After the end of the war development work began in the United States on a design to improve upon the existing models of heavy gun and carriage. A number of prototypes were produced in the 1920s and 1930s, but the projects were put on hold due to lack of funds. In 1938 the 155 mm Gun T4 on Carriage T2 was finally adopted as 155mm gun M1 on Carriage M1."}
; -- group c183 --
; [new] card "bl72(eng)" cost 1100 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x2 | vehicles bl72 | tags all artillery heavyart heavy 44 45 | units/eng/vehicles_45.set:55 | {info bl72}; copy of bl72 (with crew)
{"bl72" "In 1940 the British Army concluded that the only heavy howitzer available to it, the First World War-era BL 8-inch howitzer, had insufficient range for the conditions of the Second World War. As a stopgap the decision was made to re-line the existing barrels to a smaller calibre and develop a new range of ammunition to achieve the desired ranges. As expected, this artillery piece has devastating destructive power unrivalled by its contemporaries. Use it wisely and aim well."}
